Camera HDI configuration for the OnePlus 6 (rear IMX376K, see device/board/oneplus 0007).
- camera_host_config.hcs: one back camera lcam001 -> CAMERA_FIRST: orientation 90 (the device tree's
  270 counter-clockwise), MMAP buffers, auto exposure and white balance on, preview RGBA_8888/NV21 1280x960
  and 640x480, photo JPEG 1280x960 (the sensor's 2x2-binned 2592x1940, halved again and fitted to 4:3).
- pipeline_core/config.hcs: the pipelines name the nodes this board registers (the software nodes of the
  USB-camera VDI) instead of rk3568's RKCodec/RKScale/RKExif/RKFace.
- camss_raw.cfg (new, /vendor/etc/camera/camss_raw.cfg): which CAMSS video node, RDI subdev and sensor belong
  to the hardware name imx376; the raw format is read from the RDI pad (format=auto).
- etc/camera/CameraProfiles.json (new): the system Camera app's profiles, limited to what the HDI offers;
  without it the app falls back to a generic 4096x3072 table.

